#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# function_bijective

#% text
# `function_bijective(f, x)` gives `true` when `f` is injective and surjective (onto the reals), and `false` when it is not; `function_bijective([f, cond, ycond], x, y)` asks it from the points with `cond` onto the points with `ycond`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Injectivity and surjectivity are decided as by `function_injective` and `function_surjective`; with parameters the conditions of both are conjoined.

#% item
# A complex function with a nonzero period is not injective; a complex polynomial of one variable is injective only when it has degree 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
function_bijective(sinh(x), x)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
function_bijective(sinh(x), x, complexes)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
function_bijective([x + 2*y, 3*x - y], [x, y])
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The principal logarithm onto the strip of its values:

#% cell
[function_bijective(log(x), x, complexes), function_bijective([log(x), true, -pi < im_part(y) and im_part(y) <= pi], x, y, complexes)]
#% output
#= [false, true]

#% text
# A cubic beyond its turning points, onto the positive numbers:

#% cell
function_bijective([x^3 - x, x > 1, y > 0], x, y)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# The integers:

#% cell
function_bijective([x + 1, element(x, integers), element(y, integers)], x, y)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Options

#% cell
function_bijective(x^3 + a*x + b, x)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(true, element(a | b, reals) and a > 0)

#% cell
function_bijective(a*x, x, complexes)
#% output
#= conditional_expression(true, a != 0)

#% cell
function_bijective(a*x, x, complexes, generate_conditions: automatic)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A bijection is injective and surjective:

#% cell
[function_injective(x^3, x), function_surjective(x^3, x), function_bijective(x^3, x)]
#% output
#= [true, true, true]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Parameters give conditions, and a non-injective function is not bijective:

#% cell
[function_bijective(a*x + b, x), function_bijective(x^3 - x, x)]
#% output
#= [conditional_expression(true, element(a | b, reals) and (a > 0 or a < 0) and a != 0), false]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `function_injective`, `function_surjective`, `function_range`
